{
  "info": {
    "name": "Local Model Management",
    "description": "Exercises the Local Model Management HTTP API (apps/backend/src/models/router/models.router.ts): registry discovery, setup/provisioning (downloadAsset, separate from load), the full loadModel -> inference -> unloadModel -> close lifecycle, requestId-based cancellation, and the centralized error-handling paths.\n\nRun requests top to bottom inside a folder. `modelId` and `requestId` are captured automatically into collection variables from prior responses, so later requests just reuse `{{modelId}}` / `{{requestId}}`.\n\n**Async load/infer contract:** `POST /load` and `POST /:modelId/infer` respond immediately with `202 { requestId }` instead of waiting for the operation to finish - that's what makes them cancellable: `requestId` is in your hands while the operation is still running, so `POST /cancel/{{requestId}}` can actually race it. Poll `GET /requests/{{requestId}}` to learn the eventual outcome (`pending` -> `succeeded` | `failed` | `cancelled`). The \"start\" and \"poll until settled\" steps are separate requests in every folder below; the poll request's test script does the polling itself (loops on `GET /requests/:requestId` via `pm.sendRequest` with a 1s delay, up to 60s) so it works whether you run the folder via Collection Runner or click through it by hand. This needs a Postman client whose script sandbox supports async test scripts (`await`/`pm.sendRequest` as a promise) - recent Postman desktop/web and recent Newman do.\n\nBefore running: start the backend with `npm run dev:server` (only one QVAC-backed process at a time - stop `model-lifecycle-demo` first if it's running, the SDK locks its local storage to a single process).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3001", "type": "string" },
    {
      "key": "registryPath",
      "value": "unsloth/Qwen3-1.7B-GGUF/resolve/d7f544eead698dbd1f15126ef60b45a1e1933222/Qwen3-1.7B-Q4_0.gguf",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Same model demo.ts targets - matches @qvac/sdk's QWEN3_1_7B_INST_Q4 catalog constant."
